cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "ForkUnion: Low-latency NUMA-aware fork-join thread-pool with zero allocations, syscalls, CAS, or false-sharing on the hot path for C, C++, Rust, and Zig"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 3.0.2
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.21472186
repository-code: https://github.com/ashvardanian/ForkUnion
url: https://github.com/ashvardanian/ForkUnion
abstract: >-
  ForkUnion is a NUMA-aware fork-join thread-pool for systems languages, built for the tightest
  parallel-for loops rather than task queues. Its dispatch hot path makes no heap allocations, no
  system calls, and no compare-and-swap operations, and shares no cache line between workers, so
  fork-join latency stays flat as cores and sockets multiply. Idle workers park on a hardware address
  monitor where the processor offers one, waking the instant a peer writes the watched cache line,
  while per-domain memory placement and private per-worker cursors keep synchronization off the
  interconnect.
keywords:
  - numa
  - parallel
  - thread-pool
  - fork-join
  - allocator

